# wayland-scanner, for the build machine (G2's GP1, docs/G2-PLAN.md
# section 9): the tool that turns a protocol's XML into the C header and
# code a Wayland client or compositor compiles. A host build, from the same
# release tarball as the wayland port (host-of: the lint refuses another
# version or source), built natively with the machine's own compiler and
# installed into its stage, which is its prefix; wayland and
# wayland-protocols name it with `tool`.
#
# The build machine needs expat's headers and library (the scanner parses
# the XML with it): macOS has them in the SDK, and Ubuntu's libexpat1-dev.
# DTD validation is off (it wants libxml2): the scanner does not check the
# XML against wayland.dtd, and the protocols it runs on are upstream's.
name        wayland-scanner
version     1.26.0
revision    1
summary     wayland-scanner, built for the build machine
homepage    https://wayland.freedesktop.org/
category    tools
licence     MIT
licence-file COPYING
source      https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland/-/releases/$version/downloads/wayland-$version.tar.xz 612384 64176eaa46e4969903e286f8e5ef8331affc17fdf03ac9b58381d2b23162b7a3
place       host
host-of     wayland
style       meson
meson       -Dlibraries=false -Dscanner=true -Dtests=false -Ddocumentation=false -Ddtd_validation=false
program     bin/wayland-scanner
cpe         cpe:2.3:a:wayland:wayland
